menu "Noise core"

    config NOISE_CORE_X25519_HACL
        bool "X25519 from HACL* instead of PSA's generic curve code"
        default n
        help
            Noise's X25519 (key pairs and DH) runs on HACL* Curve25519, the
            formally verified, constant-time implementation mbedTLS ships as
            its Everest driver (tf-psa-crypto/drivers/everest), compiled from
            ESP-IDF's own copy in its 32-bit build and called directly instead
            of through PSA's generic Montgomery-curve code. Same results byte
            for byte (RFC 7748 and cacophony's Noise_XX vector,
            tests/test_noise_core.py); no protocol change.

            The Everest paths are private to ESP-IDF: on an ESP-IDF other
            than v6.0.x, or one missing any of its files, the build warns
            and Noise keeps PSA's X25519.

endmenu
